# Notion — Travel CMS (Carol edits places → site pulls)
# Create an integration at https://www.notion.so/my-integrations
# Share the "Lugares" database with that integration (read-only is enough for pull).
#
# Local:
#   npm run travel:notion:pull
#
# GitHub Actions (same values as repo Secrets):
#   Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions
#   - NOTION_TOKEN        (required for sync + deploy pull)
#   - NOTION_DATABASE_ID  (optional; defaults to Lugares id below)
#
# Workflows:
#   - "Sync travel from Notion" — cron every 6h + manual; commits snapshot + redeploys
#   - "Deploy to GitHub Pages"  — pulls Notion before build when NOTION_TOKEN is set
NOTION_TOKEN=
NOTION_DATABASE_ID=3812da8d81348023afe1ef676eb515f7

# Optional: bulk-fill Google Place ID (Places API + Geocoding)
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/places-backend.googleapis.com
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
